      communication to the public of the Work in order to protect the
      integrity of the Work and to honour or acknowledge the moral
      rights of authors or the moral rights of an author of a part of a
      Work.

2. Waiver. To the fullest extent permitted by, but not in contravention
of, applicable law, the Affirmer hereby overtly, fully, permanently,
irrevocably and unconditionally waives, abandons, and surrenders all
of the Affirmer's Copyright and Related Rights and associated claims
and causes of action, whether known or unknown (including existing as
